[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Session Management and Fast UI Login via cy.session() in Cypress"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"In modern web applications, running authentication steps before every single test can severely degrade your test suite performance. Cypress provides the cy.session() command to cache and restore cookies, localStorage, and sessionStorage, allowing you to bypass redundant login screens and achieve fast UI login."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Why Use cy.session()?"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Reduces test execution time by avoiding repetitive UI login steps."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Isolates authentication state securely across different test specs."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automatically validates session validity using a custom validation function."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Syntax and Implementation"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"The cy.session() command takes a unique session identifier, a function to setup the session (like logging in via UI), and an optional validation function to check if the session is still valid."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"cy.session('userSession', () => {
  cy.visit('/login');
  cy.get('#username').type('admin@example.com');
  cy.get('#password').type('securePassword123');
  cy.get('button[type="submit"]').click();
  cy.url().should('contain', '/dashboard');
});"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Adding a Validation Function"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"To ensure Cypress does not reuse an expired session, pass a validation function as the third argument. This function runs before every test reusing the session to verify the authentication state is intact."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"cy.session('userSession', () => {
  cy.visit('/login');
  cy.get('#username').type('admin@example.com');
  cy.get('#password').type('securePassword123');
  cy.get('button[type="submit"]').click();
  cy.url().should('contain', '/dashboard');
}, {
  validate() {
    cy.request('/api/user').its('status').should('eq', 200);
  }
});"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Using Cached Sessions in Tests"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once configured, call cy.session() at the beginning of your test or inside a beforeEach hook, followed by visiting the target page."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"describe('Dashboard Feature Tests', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    cy.session('userSession', () => {
      cy.visit('/login');
      cy.get('#username').type('admin@example.com');
      cy.get('#password').type('securePassword123');
      cy.get('button[type="submit"]').click();
    });
    cy.visit('/dashboard');
  });

  it('should display the welcome message', () => {
    cy.get('.welcome-banner').should('contain', 'Welcome, Admin');
  });
});"},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use distinct session IDs for different user roles (e.g., 'adminSession', 'guestSession')."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep session setup lean by performing API logins inside cy.session() if your app supports it, further speeding up tests."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always include a fast validation check to catch expired tokens immediately."}]
